  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO- Mozambique Country Office</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Change Resilience through Nature-based Adaptation Solutions in Mozambique is an initiative which appended to the ongoing Education programme, and it is being implemented in the Zambezia province in partnership with the ministry of Environment andLand (MTA) at central and lower levels, and covers two districts, Maganja da Costa and Milange.
The implementing structure of this initiativeis built on the existing EFAC structure. However, it incorporates two new partners, RADEZA (Rede Para Ambiente eDesenvolvimento Comunit&#xe1;rio Sustent&#xe1;vel da Zamb&#xe9;zia) as the local implementing partner, working with Climate Change Platform supporting 2 other local and district Civil Society platform named NASCIM-Nucleo das Associacoes da SC de Milange and FADMAC-F&#xf3;rumdas Associa&#xe7;&#xf5;es para o Desenvolvimento de Maganja da Costa. These partners work in an activity-based engagement, not a Grant-based collaboration.
Oxfam in Mozambique has great experience in education, gender and climate resilience and will be coordinating all the implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM HONGKONG</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib is one of the 17 national affiliates of the Oxfam International Confederation. It started life in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Working together in confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education forall, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam established this country office to support local organizations and projects.  Through this local office Oxfam Novib directly contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
